To move a file to an archive directory using `ssh.net` and the `SftpClient` class, you can use the `SftpClient.MoveFile` method. Here's an example:
```csharp
using System;
using System.IO;
using SSH.Net;

class Program
{
    static void Main(string[] args)
    {
        // Create a new SFTP client
        using (var client = new SftpClient("host"))
        {
            // Move the file to the archive directory
            client.MoveFile("source/path/to/file", "archive/directory/");
        }
    }
}
```
This will move the file located at `source/path/to/file` to the `archive/directory/` directory on the remote server.
